# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "Support for multi-process and multi-threaded acceleration for the latest version of Sample-based quantum diagonalization (SQD)"
msgstr "Sokongan untuk pecutan berbilang proses dan berbilang bebenang untuk versi terkini Sample-based quantum diagonalization (SQD)"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Support for multi-process and multi-threaded acceleration"
msgstr "Sokongan untuk pecutan berbilang proses dan berbilang bebenang"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title #
#, no-wrap
msgid "Support for multi-process and multi-threaded acceleration {#support-for-multi-process-and-multi-threaded-acceleration}"
msgstr "Sokongan untuk pecutan berbilang proses dan berbilang bebenang {#support-for-multi-process-and-multi-threaded-acceleration}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This page documents the extent to which `qiskit-addon-sqd` supports multi-threaded and multi-process acceleration, and the assumptions that a high-performance-computing (HPC) developer can rely on when integrating this package into an accelerated workload.\n"
msgstr "Halaman ini mendokumenkan setakat mana `qiskit-addon-sqd` menyokong pecutan berbilang bebenang dan berbilang proses, serta andaian yang boleh dipegang oleh pembangun pengkomputeran berprestasi tinggi (HPC) apabila mengintegrasikan pakej ini ke dalam beban kerja yang dipecutkan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "The single-threaded assumption {#the-single-threaded-assumption}"
msgstr "Andaian satu bebenang {#the-single-threaded-assumption}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Unless otherwise specified, the APIs in this package are meant to be called from a single thread. High-level APIs exposed by this package are not guaranteed to be re-entrant, and end users should not invoke them from any thread other than the main thread.\n"
msgstr "Melainkan dinyatakan sebaliknya, API dalam pakej ini bertujuan untuk dipanggil daripada satu bebenang. API peringkat tinggi yang didedahkan oleh pakej ini tidak dijamin boleh masuk semula (re-entrant), dan pengguna akhir tidak seharusnya memanggilnya daripada sebarang bebenang selain bebenang utama.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Collective multi-process execution {#collective-multi-process-execution}"
msgstr "Pelaksanaan kolektif berbilang proses {#collective-multi-process-execution}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This package supports collective multi-process acceleration in the single-program, multiple-data (SPMD) style, in which the entire program is launched as multiple isolated processes that run with explicit global synchronization and communication between them (for example, `mpirun -n 128 python my_program.py`). Because the SPMD style composes cleanly with job schedulers and other parallel software and scales to large process counts, it is the recommended model for high-performance and large-scale workloads, and it is the subject of this page.\n"
msgstr "Pakej ini menyokong pecutan kolektif berbilang proses dalam gaya satu atur cara, pelbagai data (SPMD), di mana keseluruhan atur cara dilancarkan sebagai beberapa proses terpencil yang berjalan dengan penyegerakan global dan komunikasi yang jelas antara satu sama lain (contohnya, `mpirun -n 128 python my_program.py`). Oleh sebab gaya SPMD sesuai digabungkan dengan penjadual kerja dan perisian selari yang lain serta berskala kepada bilangan proses yang besar, ia merupakan model yang disyorkan untuk beban kerja berprestasi tinggi dan berskala besar, dan ia menjadi tajuk halaman ini.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Although this package is designed to accommodate different collective-execution backends, its current implementation targets MPI, the standard message-passing API for HPC systems. Regardless of implementation, this package assumes that a single thread controls each process. In the case of MPI, this corresponds to `MPI_THREAD_FUNNELED` or lower.\n"
msgstr "Walaupun pakej ini direka untuk menampung pelbagai hujung belakang pelaksanaan kolektif, pelaksanaannya pada masa ini menyasarkan MPI, iaitu API pemesejan piawai untuk sistem HPC. Tanpa mengira pelaksanaan, pakej ini mengandaikan bahawa satu bebenang mengawal setiap proses. Dalam kes MPI, ini sepadan dengan `MPI_THREAD_FUNNELED` atau lebih rendah.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If a function supports collective execution, its documentation must say so. If the documentation does not mention collective execution, the function has no collective semantics and must be called from the control process alone.\n"
msgstr "Jika sesuatu fungsi menyokong pelaksanaan kolektif, dokumentasinya mesti menyatakannya. Jika dokumentasi tidak menyebut pelaksanaan kolektif, fungsi tersebut tidak mempunyai semantik kolektif dan mesti dipanggil daripada proses kawalan sahaja.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The specific return-value and synchronization semantics of a collective function are documented with the function itself. In general, that documentation should make clear:\n"
msgstr "Semantik nilai pulangan dan penyegerakan khusus bagi fungsi kolektif didokumenkan bersama fungsi itu sendiri. Secara amnya, dokumentasi tersebut hendaklah menjelaskan:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Whether the function is meant to be called independently by each process on its own local data, or collectively by all processes.\n"
msgstr "Sama ada fungsi itu bertujuan dipanggil secara bebas oleh setiap proses pada data tempatannya sendiri, atau secara kolektif oleh semua proses.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "How its arguments must agree across processes.\n"
msgstr "Bagaimana argumennya mesti selaras merentas proses.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "How its return value is delivered—whether the result exists only on the control process, whether all processes receive the same value, or whether each process receives a handle to a local portion of a distributed data structure.\n"
msgstr "Bagaimana nilai pulangannya disampaikan—sama ada hasilnya wujud pada proses kawalan sahaja, sama ada semua proses menerima nilai yang sama, atau sama ada setiap proses menerima pemegang kepada bahagian tempatan struktur data teragih.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Only one function currently supports being called collectively from all processes: [`diagonalize_fermionic_hamiltonian()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-addon-sqd/fermion#qiskit_addon_sqd.fermion.diagonalize_fermionic_hamiltonian \"qiskit_addon_sqd.fermion.diagonalize_fermionic_hamiltonian\"). When it is invoked collectively, the eigensolver step is where all processes participate and contribute work, so an eigensolver implementation can use every process. The remaining parts of the configuration-recovery loop have no distributed implementation and run on the control process (rank 0) only.\n"
msgstr "Pada masa ini hanya satu fungsi yang menyokong pemanggilan secara kolektif daripada semua proses: [`diagonalize_fermionic_hamiltonian()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-addon-sqd/fermion#qiskit_addon_sqd.fermion.diagonalize_fermionic_hamiltonian \"qiskit_addon_sqd.fermion.diagonalize_fermionic_hamiltonian\"). Apabila ia dipanggil secara kolektif, langkah penyelesai eigen ialah tempat semua proses mengambil bahagian dan menyumbang kerja, supaya pelaksanaan penyelesai eigen boleh menggunakan setiap proses. Bahagian lain dalam gelung pemulihan konfigurasi tidak mempunyai pelaksanaan teragih dan hanya berjalan pada proses kawalan (pangkat 0).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Every subspace of an iteration is passed to the eigensolver in a single call, so an implementation is free to divide the processes into groups and diagonalize several subspaces in parallel. How a solver uses the processes available to it is a property of that eigensolver.\n"
msgstr "Setiap subruang bagi satu lelaran dihantar kepada penyelesai eigen dalam satu panggilan, jadi pelaksanaan bebas membahagikan proses kepada kumpulan dan mempepenjurukan beberapa subruang secara selari. Bagaimana penyelesai menggunakan proses yang tersedia kepadanya ialah sifat penyelesai eigen itu.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Some existing eigensolver implementations require the calling program to run outside an MPI/SPMD environment, because they launch and manage their own parallel processes internally, for example by invoking `mpirun` on the user’s behalf. That mode is convenient for interactive and notebook-based work and remains supported; its requirements on the calling program are described in the API reference of the [`diagonalize_fermionic_hamiltonian()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-addon-sqd/fermion#qiskit_addon_sqd.fermion.diagonalize_fermionic_hamiltonian \"qiskit_addon_sqd.fermion.diagonalize_fermionic_hamiltonian\") function.\n"
msgstr "Sesetengah pelaksanaan penyelesai eigen sedia ada memerlukan atur cara pemanggil berjalan di luar persekitaran MPI/SPMD, kerana ia melancarkan dan mengurus proses selari mereka sendiri secara dalaman, contohnya dengan memanggil `mpirun` bbagi pihak pengguna. Mod itu mudah untuk kerja interaktif dan berasaskan buku nota dan terus disokong; keperluannya ke atas atur cara pemanggil diterangkan dalam rujukan API bagi fungsi [`diagonalize_fermionic_hamiltonian()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-addon-sqd/fermion#qiskit_addon_sqd.fermion.diagonalize_fermionic_hamiltonian \"qiskit_addon_sqd.fermion.diagonalize_fermionic_hamiltonian\").\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Error handling in a multi-process context {#error-handling-in-a-multi-process-context}"
msgstr "Pengendalian ralat dalam konteks berbilang proses {#error-handling-in-a-multi-process-context}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A function that is called collectively from all processes must not raise an exception or abort only a single process, because that would leave the remaining processes deadlocked or in an inconsistent state. Instead, error handling follows fail-stop semantics for the execution context as a whole: upon an error, the implementation must be prepared to abort the entire execution context collectively (for example, by using `MPI_Abort`).\n"
msgstr "Fungsi yang dipanggil secara kolektif daripada semua proses tidak boleh membangkitkan pengecualian atau menggugurkan satu proses sahaja, kerana itu akan menyebabkan proses yang selebihnya buntu atau berada dalam keadaan tidak konsisten. Sebaliknya, pengendalian ralat mengikut semantik henti-gagal bagi konteks pelaksanaan secara keseluruhan: apabila berlaku ralat, pelaksanaan mesti bersedia untuk menggugurkan keseluruhan konteks pelaksanaan secara kolektif (contohnya, dengan menggunakan `MPI_Abort`).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The API cannot guarantee coordinated error reporting or collective delivery of exceptions across processes, because MPI implementations do not provide such guarantees. An implementation might additionally attempt to make an error visible to all participating processes—for example, by having each process raise an exception—but this can only be provided on a best-effort basis and must not be relied upon for correctness or recovery.\n"
msgstr "API tidak dapat menjamin pelaporan ralat yang diselaraskan atau penyampaian pengecualian secara kolektif merentas proses, kerana pelaksanaan MPI tidak memberikan jaminan sedemikian. Sesebuah pelaksanaan mungkin turut cuba menjadikan ralat kelihatan kepada semua proses yang mengambil bahagian—contohnya, dengan meminta setiap proses membangkitkan pengecualian—tetapi ini hanya boleh disediakan secara usaha terbaik dan tidak boleh diharapkan untuk ketepatan atau pemulihan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "These are properties that a collective implementation is permitted to have, not guarantees about any particular one. In this package, the only collective step is the eigensolver (see the preceding section); its default implementation is not distributed, so these considerations apply to a custom, collective eigensolver supplied by the user.\n"
msgstr "Ini ialah sifat yang dibenarkan bagi pelaksanaan kolektif, bukan jaminan tentang mana-mana pelaksanaan tertentu. Dalam pakej ini, satu-satunya langkah kolektif ialah penyelesai eigen (lihat bahagian sebelumnya); pelaksanaan lalainya tidak teragih, jadi pertimbangan ini terpakai kepada penyelesai eigen kolektif tersuai yang dibekalkan oleh pengguna.\n"
